    <statement><p>Evaluate the double integral
 <m>\displaystyle \iint_D x^{2}y \, dA,</m>
where <m>D</m> is the top half of the disc with center the origin and radius <m>4,</m> by changing to polar coordinates.</p>
<p>Answer: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{2\cdot 4^{5}}{\left(2+1\right)\mathopen{}\left(2+3\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
